From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] IOFindBSDRoot: rd=zfs:POOL[/DATASET] waits for boot-uuid-media

Root on ZFS (P3-03, docs/architecture/filesystems.md §8). With
rd=zfs:POOL[/DATASET] and no /chosen boot-uuid, IOFindBSDRoot waited for
an IOMedia whose BSD name was "zfs:..." and never found one. It now waits
for the boot-uuid-media resource, as it does for a boot-uuid: zfs.kext
(kexts/zfs patch 0012) reads the disks' vdev labels, imports POOL and
publishes the root dataset's ZFSDatasetProxy IOMedia under that name, the
way the macOS ZFS port roots with Apple's boot-uuid. The root device is
then that proxy's /dev/diskN, and vfs_mountroot() reaches
zfs_vfs_mountroot() once the built-in file systems decline it. No
boot-uuid resource is published, so AppleFileSystemDriver doesn't start.
A /chosen boot-uuid still wins, as before.

Rebase-risk: low (one branch in the rd= parser)
---
--- a/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
@@ -861,6 +861,14 @@
 					mediaProperty = "boot-uuid-media";
 				}
 			}
+		} else if (strncmp( look, "zfs:", strlen( "zfs:" )) == 0) {
+			// rd=zfs:POOL[/DATASET]: zfs.kext imports the pool and
+			// publishes the dataset's proxy IOMedia as boot-uuid-media
+			// (kexts/zfs patch 0012), as AppleFileSystemDriver does for
+			// a boot-uuid. No boot-uuid resource: nothing else matches.
+			IOLog("rooting via ZFS: %s\n", look + strlen( "zfs:" ));
+			matching = IOUUIDMatching();
+			mediaProperty = "boot-uuid-media";
 		} else {
 			matching = IOBSDNameMatching( look );
 		}
